@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+# ATLAS Clarus moodboard integration pilot
+
+This is a source-level integration into the existing React/Tauri ArtCraft
+moodboard. It is not an externally installable plug-in and does not target the
+separate `artcraft-native` application.
+
+Base: `d4e4ac69bbd93d237eaf5d0260bc6a5ff3a5e373` (2026-10-11).
+
+## User workflow
+
+In the moodboard Grid toolbar, choose **Import ATLAS Clarus palette**, then
+select a Clarus palette JSON 1.2 file containing `source_assignments`.
+Each source occurrence becomes an ordinary ArtCraft color item using its
+original HEX. Double-click a swatch to see its ATLAS reference and recorded
+provenance in ItemInspector. Local board persistence retains both.
+
+Choose **Export ATLAS Clarus palette** to reconstruct Clarus JSON 1.2 from
+the saved source-backed records in the current board. Every saved annotation
+is revalidated before serialization. The exporter preserves source RGB, fixed
+reference identity, sampling/image provenance, master binding and NOT_SIGNED;
+it does not remap from the current design swatch.
+
+The reference-only ASE, GPL, CSS and token exports cannot reconstruct original
+RGB values. This first integration therefore accepts the rich JSON export.
+It does not add those reference-only formats or the full ColourKit startup
+envelope. ArtCraft's existing image palette extractor is unchanged.
+
+## Data contract
+
+`BoardColorItem.color` is the design color. Optional `atlasClarus` metadata
+uses schema `atlas-clarus-artcraft/0.2`:
+
+- `source_assignment`: full received original RGB/HEX, reference address,
+  row identity, master checksum, assignment rule, image and sampling record,
+  including unrecognized additional fields.
+- `reference_record`: full matching reference record, including optional Lab.
+- `import`: distinct import UUID, filename, palette name, source index,
+  format/version and SHA-256 of the exact received file bytes.
+- `reference_csv_sha256`: identity of the pinned RGB projection used to
+  check the assignment.
+
+Native ArtCraft item UUIDs identify occurrences. Two colors or repeat imports
+are never deduplicated by reference address or row id. The entire source file
+is not embedded in every item; its checksum identifies the received file,
+while the two complete relevant records retain the color provenance.
+Keep the received JSON if exact file-byte recovery is required. A pilot export
+is a newly serialized, semantically equivalent source-backed palette; it is not
+byte-for-byte recovery of the received file, and unused reference-only rows are
+not reconstructed.
+
+| Design color | Original RGB | ATLAS address | Row id | Reference RGB | Reference HEX | Squared RGB distance |
+|--------------|--------------|---------------|--------|---------------|---------------|----------------------|
+| #3D7B19      | 61, 123, 25  | H130_L045_C055 | 4966   | 55, 121, 26   | #37791A       | 41                   |
+| #3C7B19      | 60, 123, 25  | H130_L045_C055 | 4966   | 55, 121, 26   | #37791A       | 30                   |
+
+Master binding:
+`8283ab91b10f89ac758d09ecf5fb4d6343536600a06dd468b1cc1ecf4ec747c4`.
+The original frozen master is not written or regenerated. A read-only RGB
+projection of its 13,283 rows is shipped separately under its data license.
+Projection SHA-256:
+`a25f4dbd94d819ed3c9b899d0e0db7d4d9449cf8028201d0776fad93b5a7fab9`.
+
+The importer validates the full projection checksum, the master binding,
+reference identity and the nearest integer squared-sRGB distance over all
+rows (lower zero-based row id wins ties). It validates recorded image and
+sampling structure, but has no original image bytes or signature to verify.
+No physical color measurement, ICC conversion or perceptual distance is claimed.
+The synthetic two-greens fixture contains a null image checksum.
+
+The inspector rechecks saved mapping metadata instead of trusting a persisted
+success flag. If another ArtCraft action changes the design swatch, it shows
+that the stored mapping describes the imported original, preserving that
+history. It never changes the design color to the reference RGB.
+
+## Implementation and scope
+
+The importer is loaded lazily from a separate chunk. It reads at most 16 MiB,
+64 references and 4096 source records. Validation finishes before mutation.
+The store rejects a changed/deleted destination board. It preflights the
+complete persisted state in ArtCraft's existing localStorage slot before
+updating memory, so quota rejection does not create a partially imported board.
+The existing document serializer retains the optional item metadata unchanged.
+
+The desktop adapter has no remote persistence configured. Remote server
+round-trips and older app versions stripping metadata are outside this pilot's
+acceptance scope. The browser test uses the actual MoodboardWorkspace,
+BoardGridToolbar and ItemInspector, with no remote services or user account.
+It is a test host, not the installed Tauri app.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+After applying the patch to a separate checkout of the base revision:
+
+```sh
+cd frontend
+npm ci --ignore-scripts
+npx vitest run --config libs/components/moodboard/vite.config.ts
+npx tsc -b libs/components/moodboard/tsconfig.lib.json
+cd apps/artcraft
+npm run build
+```
+
+For the interactive browser host (from `frontend`):
+
+```sh
+npx vite --config tools/testing/clarus/vite.config.ts
+```
+
+Open the printed localhost address and import:
+`frontend/libs/components/moodboard/src/lib/clarus/two-greens.clarus.json`.
+The host uses a separate browser origin from the installed desktop app.
+
+For automated browser acceptance (also from `frontend`, with the manual host
+stopped), install the browser matching your Playwright version and run:
+
+```sh
+npx playwright install chromium
+node tools/testing/clarus/browser.cjs
+```
+
+The script starts/stops its own local host and uses a fresh browser context.
+`CLARUS_PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE` can point at a separately installed Playwright
+module; `CLARUS_RESULTS_DIR` chooses the result directory.
+The recorded run used Playwright 1.51.1 and Chromium 134.0.6998.35 because
+the newer browser archive was unavailable in the test environment.
+
+Acceptance: 63 Vitest tests passed (38 existing, 25 added); TypeScript project
+build passed; complete desktop frontend production build passed; seven
+browser checks passed. Existing build warnings about large chunks and mixed
+Tauri imports remain. No native Rust/Tauri binary was built or installed.
+An OS-specific build and a test in that native WebView are still required.
+
+## Source and license
+
+The integration code is newly written for this pilot under ArtCraft's
+existing source licensing terms. No GPL implementation from the ATLAS
+exporter has been copied.
+
+The read-only reference projection is sourced from
+[ATLAS Clarus Connect RC32.2](https://github.com/HelabHLC/atlas-clarus-connect/tree/e83b8165bb4c7ef4c9e37522310b9c60b7e2d19c).
+See `src/lib/clarus/REFERENCE-DATA-ZLIB.txt` in the moodboard library for
+the freieFarbe data license and conversion notice.
+The synthetic export is extracted unchanged from the upstream
+[two-greens fixture](https://github.com/HelabHLC/atlas-clarus-connect/blob/e83b8165bb4c7ef4c9e37522310b9c60b7e2d19c/browser-bundle/tests/fixtures/colour-kit-030-two-greens.json);
+its CC BY 4.0 attribution is in `EXAMPLE-NOTICE.txt`.

